#: includes/dl-method.php:47
msgid "Once a day"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: a time zone, such as America/Edmonton.
#: includes/dl-method.php:49
#, php-format
msgid "Each podcast consumer is counted at most once per episode file each calendar day, midnight to midnight in this site's time zone (%s). A podcast consumer is the IP address (an IPv6 address cut to its first 64 bits) together with the app's user agent. A podcast consumer each day is counted the same way, once across all episodes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dl-method.php:52
msgid "What is left out"
msgstr ""

#: includes/dl-method.php:53
msgid "HEAD requests; requests that only ask whether a file has changed; the two-byte test requests some apps send first (bytes 0 to 1); Apple Watch duplicates of a download on the paired phone; bots, crawlers, feed checkers and server libraries, and empty or broken user agents, using the open user agent list of the Open Podcast Analytics Working Group (OPAWG) and OP3's list of further bots; addresses of data centres, hosting companies and VPNs; and any address with more than 30 counted downloads in an hour or 100 in a day."
msgstr ""

