#: includes/listen.php:1395
msgid "When you play the audio reading of a post, this site measures how the reading is listened to: when it is played and paused, which parts are heard, changes of speed and volume, jumps forward or back, whether it is heard to the end, how far down the page you scroll, how long the page is open, the site or link that brought you here (only the site's name and any campaign tag on the link), whether you use a phone, tablet or computer, and your country."
msgstr ""

#: includes/listen.php:1396
msgid "This is measured by this site itself. Nothing is sent to any other company, and no cookies are used for it. Your IP address is never stored: it is combined with your browser's name and scrambled with a random code that is replaced and thrown away every day, so the result cannot be traced back to you or linked from one day to the next. Your country is worked out from your IP address at the moment of the visit, and only the country is kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/listen.php:1398
msgid "If your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal, none of this is measured."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: (int) $l['events_days'], 2: (int) $l['sessions_days'].
#: includes/listen.php:1400
#, php-format
msgid "The detailed record of each visit is deleted after %1$d days, and each visit's summary after %2$d days. Daily totals, which contain nothing about any one visitor, are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/listen.php:1402
msgid "Countries are looked up with IP Geolocation by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com), used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of months.
#: includes/listen.php:1407
#, php-format
msgid "To tell new listeners from returning ones, after you listen for 30 seconds your browser keeps the month in its own storage on your device. On a later visit within %d month, the player tells this site only that you have listened here before, never when. You can remove it by clearing this site's data in your browser."
msgid_plural "To tell new listeners from returning ones, after you listen for 30 seconds your browser keeps the month in its own storage on your device. On a later visit within %d months, the player tells this site only that you have listened here before, never when. You can remove it by clearing this site's data in your browser."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: includes/listen.php:1423
msgid "When you play an audio reading, this site also tells Google Analytics that a reading was started, reached halfway or was heard to the end, with the reading's title. Google Analytics is subject to Google's own privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/listen.php:1426
msgid "When a podcast app downloads an episode, this site counts the download and notes which app and kind of device it was, worked out from the app's name, following the IAB Tech Lab podcast measurement guidelines. The IP address is never stored: it is scrambled with a random code that is replaced every day, only to count each listener once a day, and is checked against a list of data centre and VPN networks, which this site downloads once a month (nothing about visitors is sent to get it). For members' private feeds the member is counted the same way, and only totals are kept, never which member downloaded what."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: a list of host names, such as op3.dev.
#: includes/listen.php:1434
#, php-format
msgid "Podcast apps reach this site's episodes through %s first, which counts downloads for this podcast and sees the app's IP address and name, as any web server does. Those services have their own privacy policies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/listen.php:1440
msgid "When a new episode is added to this site's podcast feed, the site tells Podcast Index and a public WebSub hub run by Google the feed's address, so podcast apps learn of it sooner. Nothing about visitors or listeners is sent."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the hub's host name.
#: includes/listen.php:1442
#, php-format
msgid "When a new episode is added to this site's podcast feed, the site tells Podcast Index and the WebSub hub at %s the feed's address, so podcast apps learn of it sooner. Nothing about visitors or listeners is sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/listen.php:1446
msgid "If you are a member, your account has its own podcast feed address, made of a random code kept with your account. The feed itself contains nothing about you. Podcast apps that fetch it on their own servers see only the address."
