#: views/teleprompter.php:611
msgid "Struck through: skipped. Wavy underline: misread (hover, or move to it with the arrow keys, to hear what was heard; Flagged moments lists it too). Dashed underline: worth a listen, where Whisper heard a slightly different form of the word, such as “coming” for “come.” These are often Whisper’s mistake, so they don’t count against your accuracy. Small rounded tags: words that were added, repeated, or filler. Shaded sentences were rushed, slow, or wandered from the script, and each starts with a small tag saying which (slow ones also have a dotted edge). A dotted underline means a flat sentence, and an arrow marks a faded ending. A gold tilde is a fade you marked, which is never flagged. With Show pauses on, each pause of a second or more shows its length: plain between sentences, underlined at a paragraph break, and in a box inside a sentence. The percentage beside each paragraph is how much of it was read as written. Click any word to hear it. From the keyboard, Tab to the script: left and right move word by word and Enter plays from the word. Space plays and pauses, Escape returns to the teleprompter. The timeline above repeats Flagged moments, whose buttons are the keyboard way in."
msgstr ""

#: views/teleprompter.php:612
msgid "With Edit audio on, clicking selects instead of playing: drag across words or shift-click to select more, double-click for a whole sentence, triple-click for the whole paragraph, and Shift with the arrow keys starts a selection at the word cursor or makes it a word longer or shorter. Cut (or Delete) takes the selection out of the audio, and Retake records it again: the old words are taken out from where your voice really starts to where it stops, and anything you say before or after the selected words in the retake is trimmed away. A gold double strike marks a cut, a gold bar under words marks a retake, and a shortened pause shows its old and new length. Click a cut word to bring it back. Click a retaken word to open its retake again: Start and End move each side of the splice 10 ms at a time, cutting more or less of the old reading (the [ and ] keys do the same, with Shift for the end). If a word is heard twice at a join, such as “picture-icture”, cut more of the old reading on that side. Space before and Space after add a pause at a join, 50 ms at a time, filled with your room’s own background. Each step plays the join so you hear it at once, Reset puts everything back, and Bring back the original takes the retake out. Nothing changes your recording: Make edited MP3 builds a new file from it, with the captions and chapters moved to match."
msgstr ""

#: views/teleprompter.php:613
msgid "Whisper sometimes mishears unusual words such as names and specialist terms, or tidies away ums and stumbles. When it gets something wrong, use “I said it right” and it will remember. Treat the counts as a guide and your ears as the judge."
msgstr ""

